  "overview": "Henry Nowak’s family speak for the first time.  In this documentary, they say they may have been “manipulated in their darkest hours” by both Hampshire and Isle of Wight Constabulary and the police watchdog in the months following his murder.  Bodycam footage shows the officers arresting Henry as he lay dying on the ground.  The family has spoken to ITV News’ UK Editor Paul Brand about the way Henry was treated and their own dealings with the police in the months after his death.",
